      "sourceTextSha256": "25bbc55cce58841575caaeddb102190c1d09975a0eb4a6e45ea9d12278c9121e",
      "text": "Day 8 · Breakfast, then the Cocora Valley (7 hours): a welcome canelazo and an introduction to the Cocora Nature Reserve by a specialised eco-guide, a walk into the cloud forest, and the wax palm, the world’s tallest palm and Colombia’s national tree, with the traditional Quindío wax palm ritual and the planting of palm seedlings. Continue to Salento for a walk through its colonial streets, craft workshops and the Cocora viewpoint. Optional lunch: USD 25 per person.",
